  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing and Strengthening Tuberculosis services in Key populations across Guyana - Guyana (01-Apr-2016-31-Mar-2019)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Guyana, Tuberculosis, Ministry of Health of the Co-operative Republic of Guyana (MOH)This program has the following goals: Reduce the burden of TB by improved management of TB/HIV co-infection. To reduce TB/HIV co-infection to under 10% by 2018.  Reduce the emergence of MDR-TB by improving case detection (of over 90% of MDR-TB cases) and first line treatment success rate (to over 85% by 2018).  Reduce the transmission of TB by higher cases detection (from 75% in 2013 to over 90% in 2018) and treatment of cases. The objectives of this program are: Early diagnosis of tuberculosis including universal drug-susceptibility testing.  Improve treatment and support of all TB cases including drug-resistant tuberculosis.  Increase screening of TB contacts and high-risk groups.  Strengthen collaborative TB/HIV and other co-morbid related activities</narrative>
  </description>
